{"signature": "{\"text\": \"Here is a GCSE-style question. Fibreglass and wool felt are used for loft insulation. A thicker layer of wool felt is needed to give the same insulation as fibreglass. Part A, worth two marks: which material has the higher thermal conductivity, and why? Wool felt has the higher conductivity, so a greater thickness is needed to achieve a similar resistance to conduction. Award one mark for wool felt and one for the explanation. Part B, worth two marks: explain why trapped air helps reduce energy transfer. Air has low thermal conductivity, so conduction through it is slow; trapping the air in small pockets also prevents large convection currents. Award one mark for each correct explanation.\", \"voice\": \"en-NG-AbeoNeural\", \"rate\": \"-4%\", \"eleven\": false}", "duration": 46.632, "words": [["Here", 0.102083], ["is", 0.3495], ["a", 0.466666], ["GCSE-style", 0.583875], ["question.", 1.44325], ["Fibreglass", 2.838541], ["and", 3.59375], ["wool", 3.763041], ["felt", 3.89325], ["are", 4.231791], ["used", 4.388041], ["for", 4.6745], ["loft", 4.84375], ["insulation.", 5.234375], ["A", 6.796875], ["thicker", 6.992208], ["layer", 7.291666], ["of", 7.539083], ["wool", 7.734375], ["felt", 7.890625], ["is", 8.26825], ["needed", 8.4375], ["to", 8.763041], ["give", 8.919291], ["the", 9.140625], ["same", 9.270833], ["insulation", 9.505208], ["as", 10.052083], ["fibreglass.", 10.247416], ["Part", 11.979166], ["A,", 12.252625], ["worth", 12.734375], ["two", 13.033875], ["marks:", 13.190125], ["which", 13.880208], ["material", 14.101583], ["has", 14.570333], ["the", 14.804708], ["higher", 14.908875], ["thermal", 15.2995], ["conductivity,", 15.625], ["and", 16.692708], ["why?", 16.901041], ["Wool", 18.098958], ["felt", 18.333333], ["has", 18.658875], ["the", 18.854166], ["higher", 18.945333], ["conductivity,", 19.335958], ["so", 20.351583], ["a", 20.546875], ["greater", 20.677083], ["thickness", 21.054708], ["is", 21.484375], ["needed", 21.640625], ["to"